l_test_paths/last_review_record/mechanical_close_attestation/work_tip/governing_rev/governing_identity/format_trailer/parse_trailer/round_file/session_log/format_scope/gating_span/filing_refusal/branch_paths/logged_rounds/round_entries/branch_entries/tree_already_judged/declared_phases/phases_owed/round_count/_closed_wi_ids/mechanical_close_subject/format_branch_trailer/branch_trailers;attest/_attest_preflight/_attest_message/_lane_off_trunk/_harness_floor_refusal/_attest_commit/_bar_refusal/_lane_mark_refusal/_run_review_bar/_unstaged_dirt/_AttestPlan\\\"'\nonce 'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' \"'$old $new\nonce '\"'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' 'Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract.\\\"\\\"\\\"' 'Readers treat unavailable repository answers according to their own fail-closed contract. The attest route reads the declared expected-failure mark with the review bar from one parse of the attested lane''s declarations, with no default, and refuses before either bar when either required declaration is unavailable. Its mark-transition refusal reads the newest verified review attestation in the lane range, or the lane base when none exists, and preserves branch and index on every refusal.\\\"\\\"\\\"'\nonce 'docs/test/test-cases.toml' 'or the message is unreadable or carries the label; a hook refusal or rewrite after a green bar is undone, leaving branch and index unchanged;' 'or the message is unreadable or carries the label; an unavailable declared expected-failure mark or an invalid mark transition refuses before the bar, leaving branch and index unchanged; a hook refusal or rewrite after a green bar is undone, leaving branch and index unchanged;'\nonce 'docs/test/test-cases.toml' 'via the LLR-140 claim/integration contract and the LLR-207 attest, producer and refresh-attestation contract\\\"' 'via the LLR-140 claim/integration contract and the LLR-207 attest, producer and refresh-attestation contract, including the declared expected-failure-mark refusal\\\"'\n\"'$llr=@'\"'\n[design.LLR-368]\nsr_refs = [\\\"SR-156\\\"]\ntitle = \\\"Expected-failure marks are declared, attested, and excluded from landing trees\\\"\nmodule = \\\"project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/red_mark.py;project-trajectory/scripts/integrate.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/verdict.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/git.py;project-trajectory/scripts/kitlib/spine.py\\\"\ncode_symbol = \\\"read_bars/Bars/Bars.refusal/count/tree_counts/findings/attest_refusal/landing_refusal;attest/_attest_preflight/_lane_mark_refusal/_AttestPlan/refresh;normal_test_paths/last_review_record;read_blobs/write_blobs;declared_roots\\\"\ndetail = \\\"The expected-failure mark is one declared non-empty stripped text beside the review bar, with no default or fallback, and both are read from one parse of the tree the verb runs on; every unavailable declaration state names the declaration, key, and cause, and when both keys are unavailable each is named. The shipped declaration carries the reference text without an at-sign and explains its required, whitespace-insensitive, other-stack, helper, and every-adopter rules. Test files are regular files beneath the declared test root as resolved for the review set, excluding links and submodules. Counts are non-overlapping byte occurrences after ASCII whitespace is removed from the declared text and file bytes, so wrapped and parameter marks count without decoding. The reference is the newest verified review attestation in the lane range, or the lane base with no record; a test-set entry names a path only after digest normalization, never when it is a node id or directory. Equal counts are not judged. A raised count passes only when its test set names the path; a lowered count on a present path passes only when a verified reference record covers the same test set and the set names the path, otherwise each refusal names the path and failed condition; a lowered count on an absent path is not judged. An unreadable range, reference tree, or staged tree refuses naming the read. Every refusal precedes the bar and leaves branch and index unchanged. A removal made by a plain commit is judged at the next attestation. Before either refresh bar, the tree it bars refuses every marked test file with its count; a mark-free tree refreshes unchanged, a refused refresh keeps the lane at its work tip, and a refresh reads a merged declaration. Files brought by a merge-refresh are not judged; a partial close holding a mark is refused, quarantined, then refreshed; rebasing changes the base reference; and a bootstrapped scaffold receives its declaration from the template. The repository test root holds no mark in a landing tree. Coverage bound: D31 to D35 are inside and driven by TC-421 to TC-426; D37 to D41 are outside and not tested here; D42 is the rebase case.\\\"\ntest_refs = \\\"TC-421; TC-422; TC-423; TC-424; TC-425; TC-426\\\"\nstatus = \\\"Drafted\\\"\ncomponent = \\\"CMP-008\\\"\nphase = 6\n'@\nappend 'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml' 'LLR-368' \"'$llr\n$tc=@'\"'\n[test.TC-421]\nverifies = [\\\"SR-156\\\", \\\"LLR-368\\\", \\\"IF-022\\\"]\nlevel = \\\"Unit\\\"\nmethod = \\\"Run declaration unit cases for the declared expected-failure mark.\\\"\ntier = \\\"Smoke\\\"\nexpected = \\\"A non-empty stripped declaration is accepted; every unavailable state names the declaration, key, and cause; both unavailable keys are named; one parse supplies both values; and the shipped declaration carries the stated reference and guidance.\\\"\nautomated = \\\"Yes\\\"\nevidence = \\\"(owed by the tests commit)\\\"\nstatus = \\\"Drafted\\\"\nphase = 6\n\n[test.TC-422]\nverifies = [\\\"SR-156\\\", \\\"LLR-368\\\"]\nlevel = \\\"Unit\\\"\nmethod = \\\"Run test-root and mark-counting unit cases.\\\"\ntier = \\\"Smoke\\\"\nexpected = \\\"Only regular files under the resolved test root count; counting is byte-based, whitespace-insensitive, non-